# Implementation Plan - Phase 3: Configurations & Architecture

## Architecture & Tech Stack
- **Target Fork**: https://github.com/pplupo/taskwarrior-webui (branch `phase3-configs`)
- **Backend**: Node.js, Koa.js, TypeScript, taskwarrior-lib CLI wrapper.
- **Frontend**: Vue 2 (Composition API), Nuxt.js, Vuetify (Material Design), Vuex (typed-vuex).

## Proposed Architectural Modules

### 1. Reverse Proxy & Deployment Configuration (#88, #92)
- **Base Path Routing (`#88`)**:
  - `frontend/nuxt.config.js`:
    - Read `process.env.ROUTER_BASE_PATH` (default `/`), configuring `router: { base: basePath }`.
    - Configure `axios: { baseURL: basePath === '/' ? '/' : `${basePath}/` }`.
    - Set up proxy or API rewrite so calls to `${basePath}api` forward to backend.
  - `backend/src/app.ts`:
    - Support base path prefix mounting in Koa router if specified via `process.env.ROUTER_BASE_PATH`, or allow matching both `/api/...` and `${basePath}api/...`.
  - `nginx/server.conf` & `docker/start.sh`:
    - Update `start.sh` and Nginx template to support environment variables `PORT` (default 80) and `ROUTER_BASE_PATH` (default `/`).
- **Configurable Port (`#92`)**:
  - `backend/src/app.ts`:
    - Read `process.env.PORT` (or `APP_PORT`), defaulting to 3000.
  - `docker/start.sh`:
    - Substitute `$PORT` into `/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf` (listen on `$PORT`).

### 2. Multi-Profile Architecture (#96)
- **Backend Profile Manager (`backend/src/profiles.ts` & `backend/src/taskwarrior.ts`)**:
  - Parse `process.env.TASK_PROFILES` (format: `Name:rc_path:data_path,Name2:rc_path2:data_path2` or JSON).
  - Default profile: `Default` using `process.env.TASKRC || '/.taskrc'` and `process.env.TASKDATA || '/.task'`.
  - Provide helper `getTaskwarrior(profileName?: string): TaskwarriorLib` that caches instances by profile.
  - Add middleware to extract profile from `X-Taskwarrior-Profile` request header or query parameter `profile`.
  - Endpoints in `backend/src/profiles.ts`:
    - `GET /config/profiles`: returns list of available profile names and default profile.
- **Frontend Profile Switching**:
  - Store state `currentProfile` and `profiles` list in `frontend/store/index.ts`.
  - Fetch profiles on initial load; if `profiles.length > 1`, display Profile selector in `frontend/layouts/default.vue`.
  - Axios interceptor in Nuxt plugin/store attaching `X-Taskwarrior-Profile` to outgoing requests.
  - Persist selection to `localStorage.getItem('taskwarrior_profile')`.

### 3. Context Support (#18)
- **Backend Context Endpoints (`backend/src/contexts.ts`)**:
  - `GET /config/contexts`: runs `task _context` to list contexts, and `task _get rc.context` to get active context.
  - `POST /config/contexts`: accepts `{ context: string }`. Runs `task context <name>` (or `task context none` if empty/none).
  - Context override in `taskwarrior-lib` execution: if `X-Taskwarrior-Context` header is present, pass `rc.context=<name>` to Taskwarrior CLI invocations.
- **Frontend Context UI**:
  - Store state `activeContext` and `contexts` list.
  - Top-bar Context menu/select in `frontend/layouts/default.vue` showing currently active context and dropdown to switch context or clear context.
  - When switched, invoke `POST /config/contexts` and reload task lists.

### 4. Sub-Projects Hierarchical Filtering (#43)
- **Filter State & Logic (`frontend/pages/index.vue`, `frontend/components/TaskList.vue`)**:
  - Add `includeSubprojects` boolean ref/state in `pages/index.vue` and `TaskList.vue`.
  - Add a toggle switch `v-switch` or button next to Project filter: "Include subprojects".
  - In `filteredTasks`:
    - When `includeSubprojects` is true and `selectedProject` is set:
      `t.project === selectedProject || (t.project && t.project.startsWith(selectedProject + '.'))`
    - When `includeSubprojects` is false:
      `t.project === selectedProject`
  - Sync `includeSubprojects` with route query `?subprojects=1` for URL persistence and sharing.

## Verification Strategy
- Run unit/typecheck tests on backend: `npm run build` in `backend/`.
- Run Nuxt build on frontend: `npm run build` in `frontend/`.
- Verify port and base path variables (`PORT=8080`, `ROUTER_BASE_PATH=/tasks`).
- Verify multi-profile retrieval and context endpoints via backend routing tests.
- Verify subproject filtering logic with tasks belonging to `project:work` and `project:work.subproject`.
